        "question_V9mANB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What piercings can twisted barbells be used for?",
            "answer": "<p>Twisted barbells are versatile and can be worn in a range of piercings including <strong>lobe, helix, conch, lip, nipple</strong>, and <strong>eyebrow piercings</strong>. Their spiral design makes them a popular choice for double or multi-hole<br/>piercings, creating a stylish twist effect.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_BYtzjc": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are twisted barbells suitable for new piercings?",
            "answer": "<p><strong>Titanium twisted barbells</strong> are safe for fresh piercings because they’re hypoallergenic and lightweight. <strong>Steel, silver, and UV coated</strong> options are recommended for healed piercings only, as silver can oxidise and UV<br/>coatings are not ideal for new piercings.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_AkGqPd": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What’s the benefit of a twisted barbell compared to a straight or curved one?",
            "answer": "<p>The twisted design offers a unique visual style and flexible fit. It’s ideal for multiple piercings in close proximity (like double lip or ear piercings) and provides a secure, comfortable feel with added aesthetic appeal.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_JjGUKX": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is UV/steel jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>UV/steel twisted barbells feature <strong>UV-reactive acrylic ends</strong> paired with <strong>surgical steel posts</strong>. They’re lightweight, fun, and glow under blacklight — perfect for customers who love a playful or colourful look.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
